From dc6aa94af60d826d95f2b5c656da3f1c83e6bfa3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: stephan-xyz <stephan@zehrer.xyz>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 15:43:40 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 33/34] bcm2835-sdiod: regulatory data, scan, WPA2 join with
 the firmware supplicant

After the firmware answers: load the CLM blob (clmload in 1400-byte
chunks), turn on the join, link, supplicant and scan events, roam_off,
WLC_UP, run an escan and list the networks found (BSSID, channel, signal,
security, name). With /etc/net/wifi (ssid=, psk=) it joins that network:
WPA2-PSK through the firmware supplicant (sup_wpa, WLC_SET_WSEC_PMK) and
waits for link up and PSK_SUP keyed, or an open network.

The control channel now collects firmware events and replies by request
ID, sends frames above 512 bytes in block mode and waits for credit.
Unit tests for events and scan results (both possible BSS layouts).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
